findings.comment:
The following structural issues were observed during the pre-opening and remain to be corrected by the next routine inspection: 
1) Loose corner trim at the wall to the right of the front service line before the drive thru needs to be sealed back to the wall - PIC reattached during inspection by screwing Nudo board back into drywall;
2) Holes in the wall behind the drive thru order screen need to be sealed;
3) Floor at left side of walk-in cooler door needs to be sealed so it is flush with the wall to eliminate the gap; and
4) Holes in wall behind the 3 part sink need to be sealed.

findings.citation_text:
6-501.11 The following structural issues were observed during the pre-opening and remain to be corrected by the next routine inspection: 
1) Loose corner trim at the wall to the right of the front service line before the drive thru needs to be sealed back to the wall - PIC reattached during inspection by screwing Nudo board back into drywall;
2) Holes in the wall behind the drive thru order screen need to be sealed;
3) Floor tiles in front of fryers with low grout are holding debris and need to be re-grouted; 
4) Floor at left side of walk-in cooler door needs to be sealed so it is flush with the wall to eliminate the gap; and
5) Holes in wall behind the 3 part sink need to be sealed. 
Physical facilities shall be maintained in good repair.
